<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian P-Notes - Tenders total A$180 mln.</title>
<headline>Australian P-Notes - Tenders total A$180 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian commercial paper market saw a busy start to the week, largely as a continuation of the rollover of promissory note maturities, traders said.</p>
<p>Seven tenders were reported totalling A$180 million.</p>
<p>The largest was for Boral which got away A$70 million of September 16 dated paper after originally offering A$40 million. Traders said A$10 million went off at 5.33 percent and the remainder fetched 5.34 percent.</p>
<p>The Barley Board made a further entry into the market after its two tenders last week, offering A$20 million for September 15, which is reported to have fetched a yield of 5.31 percent, traders added.</p>
